\p \v 8 \w The LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w and Aaron|strong="H175"\w*, \v 9 “\w When|strong="H3588"\w* \w Pharaoh|strong="H6547"\w* \w tells you|strong="H1696"\w*, ‘\w Perform|strong="H5414"\w* \w a miracle|strong="H4159"\w*,’ \w you are to say|strong="H559"\w* \w to Aaron|strong="H175"\w*, ‘\w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w your staff|strong="H4294"\w* \w and throw it down|strong="H7993"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w Pharaoh|strong="H6547"\w*,’ \w and it will become|strong="H1961"\w* \w a serpent|strong="H8577"\w*.\f + \fr 7:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa tannin\ft ; here and in verse 10, in contrast to Moses’ staff, which became a \fqa nachash\ft in \ref Exodus 4:3|EXO 4:3\ref* and was noted again in Exodus 7:15\f*”
