\p \v 14 \w And this|strong="H2088"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w will be|strong="H1961"\w* \w a memorial|strong="H2146"\w* for you, \w and you are to celebrate|strong="H2287"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w* \w as a feast|strong="H2282"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w as a permanent|strong="H5769"\w* \w statute|strong="H2708"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*. \v 15 \w For seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w you must eat|strong="H398"\w* \w unleavened bread|strong="H4682"\w*. \w On the first|strong="H7223"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w you are to remove|strong="H7673"\w* \w the leaven|strong="H7603"\w* \w from your houses|strong="H1004"\w*. \w Whoever|strong="H3605"\w* \w eats|strong="H398"\w* \w anything leavened|strong="H2557"\w* \w from the first|strong="H7223"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w through|strong="H5704"\w* \w the seventh|strong="H7637"\w* \w must be cut off|strong="H3772"\w* \w from Israel|strong="H3478"\w*.
