\p \v 17 \w So you are to keep|strong="H8104"\w* \w the Feast of Unleavened Bread|strong="H4682"\w*,\f + \fr 12:17 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten\f* \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w on this|strong="H2088"\w* \w very|strong="H6106"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w I brought|strong="H3318"\w* \w your divisions|strong="H6635"\w* \w out of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*. \w You must keep|strong="H8104"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w as a permanent|strong="H5769"\w* \w statute|strong="H2708"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*. \v 18 \w In the first month|strong="H7223"\w* \w you are to eat|strong="H398"\w* \w unleavened bread|strong="H4682"\w*, \w from the evening|strong="H6153"\w* \w of the fourteenth|strong="H702"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w the evening|strong="H6153"\w* \w of the twenty-first|strong="H259"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*. \v 19 \w For seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w there must be no|strong="H3808"\w* \w leaven|strong="H7603"\w* \w found|strong="H4672"\w* \w in your houses|strong="H1004"\w*. \w If|strong="H3588"\w* \w anyone|strong="H3605"\w* \w eats|strong="H398"\w* \w something leavened|strong="H2557"\w*, \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \w person|strong="H5315"\w*, \w whether a foreigner|strong="H1616"\w* \w or native|strong="H249"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w*, \w must be cut off|strong="H3772"\w* \w from the congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \v 20 \w You are not|strong="H3808"\w* \w to eat|strong="H398"\w* \w anything|strong="H3605"\w* \w leavened|strong="H2557"\w*; \w eat|strong="H398"\w* \w unleavened bread|strong="H4682"\w* \w in all|strong="H3605"\w* \w your homes|strong="H4186"\w*.”
