\p \v 22 \w On the sixth|strong="H8345"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*, \w they gathered|strong="H3950"\w* \w twice|strong="H4932"\w* \w as much food|strong="H3899"\w* — \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w omers|strong="H6016"\w* \w per person|strong="H259"\w*\f + \fr 16:22 \fqa 2 omers\ft is \ref approximately 4|4\ref* dry quarts or 4.4 liters per person.\f* — \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the leaders|strong="H5387"\w* \w of the congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w came|strong="H935"\w* \w and reported|strong="H5046"\w* \w this to Moses|strong="H4872"\w*. \v 23 \w He told them|strong="H559"\w*, “\w This|strong="H1931"\w* \w is what|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has said|strong="H1696"\w*: ‘\w Tomorrow|strong="H4279"\w* \w is to be a day of complete rest|strong="H7677"\w*, \w a holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \w So|strong="H853"\w* \w bake|strong="H644"\w* \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w you want to bake|strong="H644"\w*, \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w boil|strong="H1310"\w* \w what|strong="H834"\w* \w you want to boil|strong="H1310"\w*. \w Then set aside|strong="H5117"\w* \w whatever|strong="H3605"\w* \w remains|strong="H5736"\w* \w and keep it|strong="H4931"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w morning|strong="H1242"\w*.’”
