\s1 The Jar of Manna
\p \v 31 \w Now the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w called the bread|strong="H7121"\w* \w manna|strong="H4478"\w*.\f + \fr 16:31 \fqa Manna \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa What is it? \ft (see verse 15).\f* \w It|strong="H1931"\w* \w was white|strong="H3836"\w* \w like coriander|strong="H1407"\w* \w seed|strong="H2233"\w* \w and tasted|strong="H2940"\w* \w like wafers|strong="H6838"\w* \w made with honey|strong="H1706"\w*. \v 32 \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w This|strong="H2088"\w* \w is what|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has commanded|strong="H6680"\w*: ‘\w Keep|strong="H4931"\w* \w an omer|strong="H6016"\w* \w of manna|strong="H4480"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*, \w so that|strong="H4616"\w* \w they may see|strong="H7200"\w* \w the bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w I fed|strong="H398"\w* \w you in the wilderness|strong="H4057"\w* \w when I brought you|strong="H3318"\w* \w out of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*.’”
