\p \v 13 \w The next day|strong="H4283"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w took his seat|strong="H3427"\w* \w to judge|strong="H8199"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w and they stood|strong="H5975"\w* \w around|strong="H5921"\w* \w him|strong="H4872"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w morning|strong="H1242"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w evening|strong="H6153"\w*. \v 14 \w When his|strong="H4872"\w* \w father-in-law|strong="H2859"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Moses|strong="H1931"\w* \w was doing|strong="H6213"\w* \w for the people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w he asked|strong="H559"\w*, “\w What|strong="H4100"\w* \w is this|strong="H2088"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w you are|strong="H859"\w* \w doing|strong="H6213"\w* \w for the people|strong="H5971"\w*? \w Why|strong="H4069"\w* \w do you|strong="H859"\w* \w sit|strong="H3427"\w* \w alone as judge|strong="H905"\w*, \w with all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w standing|strong="H5324"\w* \w around|strong="H5921"\w* \w you from|strong="H4480"\w* \w morning|strong="H1242"\w* \w till|strong="H5704"\w* \w evening|strong="H6153"\w*?”
