\p \v 5 \w But if|strong="H518"\w* \w the servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w declares|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w I love|strong="H157"\w* \w my master|strong="H113"\w* \w and my wife|strong="H802"\w* \w and children|strong="H1121"\w*; \w I do not|strong="H3808"\w* \w want to go|strong="H3318"\w* \w free|strong="H2670"\w*,’ \v 6 \w then his master|strong="H113"\w* \w is to bring him|strong="H5066"\w* \w before|strong="H413"\w* \w the judges|strong="H430"\w*.\f + \fr 21:6 \ft Or \fqa before God\f* \w And he shall take him|strong="H5066"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the door|strong="H1817"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w doorpost|strong="H4201"\w* \w and pierce|strong="H7527"\w* \w his ear|strong="H241"\w* \w with an awl|strong="H4836"\w*. \w Then he shall serve his master|strong="H5647"\w* \w for life|strong="H5769"\w*.
\p \v 7 \w And if|strong="H3588"\w* \w a man|strong="H376"\w* \w sells|strong="H4376"\w* \w his daughter|strong="H1323"\w* \w as a servant|strong="H519"\w*, \w she is not|strong="H3808"\w* \w to go free|strong="H3318"\w* \w as the menservants do|strong="H5650"\w*. \v 8 \w If|strong="H518"\w* \w she is displeasing|strong="H7451"\w* \w in the eyes|strong="H5869"\w* \w of her master|strong="H113"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w had designated her for himself|strong="H3259"\w*,\f + \fr 21:8 \ft Or \fqa so that he does not designate her for himself\f* \w he must allow her to be redeemed|strong="H6299"\w*. \w He has no|strong="H3808"\w* \w right|strong="H4910"\w* \w to sell her|strong="H4376"\w* \w to foreigners|strong="H5971"\w*, \w since he has broken faith|strong="H898"\w* with her. \v 9 \w And if|strong="H518"\w* \w he chooses her|strong="H3259"\w* \w for his son|strong="H1121"\w*, \w he must deal|strong="H6213"\w* with her \w as with|strong="H4941"\w* \w a daughter|strong="H1323"\w*. \v 10 \w If|strong="H518"\w* \w he takes|strong="H3947"\w* \w another wife|strong="H312"\w*, \w he must not|strong="H3808"\w* \w reduce|strong="H1639"\w* \w the food|strong="H7607"\w*, \w clothing|strong="H3682"\w*, \w or marital rights of his first wife|strong="H5772"\w*. \v 11 \w If, however|strong="H518"\w*, \w he does not|strong="H3808"\w* \w provide|strong="H6213"\w* her \w with these|strong="H428"\w* \w three things|strong="H7969"\w*, \w she is free to go|strong="H3318"\w* \w without|strong="H369"\w* \w monetary payment|strong="H3701"\w*.
\s1 Personal Injury Laws
\p \v 12 \w Whoever strikes|strong="H5221"\w* \w and kills|strong="H4191"\w* \w a man|strong="H376"\w* \w must surely be put to death|strong="H4191"\w*. \v 13 \w If, however|strong="H834"\w*, \w he did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w lie in wait|strong="H6658"\w*, \w but God|strong="H430"\w* \w allowed it to happen|strong="H579"\w*, \w then I will appoint|strong="H7760"\w* for you \w a place|strong="H4725"\w* \w where|strong="H834"\w* \w he may flee|strong="H5127"\w*.
