\p \v 15 \w You are to keep|strong="H8104"\w* \w the Feast|strong="H2282"\w* \w of Unleavened Bread|strong="H4682"\w*\f + \fr 23:15 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see \ref Exodus 12:14–20|EXO 12:14-20\ref*.\f* \w as|strong="H834"\w* \w I commanded you|strong="H6680"\w*: \w At the appointed time|strong="H4150"\w* \w in the month|strong="H2320"\w* \w of Abib|strong="H24"\w*\f + \fr 23:15 \fqa Abib \ft was the first month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April.\f* \w you are to eat|strong="H398"\w* \w unleavened bread|strong="H4682"\w* \w for seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* that was the month \w you came out|strong="H3318"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*. \w No one|strong="H3808"\w* \w may appear|strong="H7200"\w* \w before Me|strong="H6440"\w* \w empty-handed|strong="H7387"\w*.
