\p \w And keep the Feast|strong="H2282"\w* \w of Ingathering|strong="H614"\w*\f + \fr 23:16 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is later called \fqa the Feast of Tabernacles \ft (or \fqa Booths \ft or \fqa Shelters\ft ).\f* \w at the end|strong="H3318"\w* \w of the year|strong="H8141"\w*, \w when you gather|strong="H622"\w* \w your produce|strong="H4639"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the field|strong="H7704"\w*.
