\s1 The Ark of the Covenant
\r (\ref Exodus 37:1–5|EXO 37:1-5\ref*)
\p \v 10 \w And they are to construct|strong="H6213"\w* \w an ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w*, \w two|strong="H520"\w* \w and a half cubits|strong="H2677"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w*, \w a cubit|strong="H520"\w* \w and a half|strong="H2677"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*, \w and a cubit|strong="H520"\w* \w and a half|strong="H2677"\w* \w high|strong="H6967"\w*.\f + \fr 25:10 \ft The ark was \ref approximately 3|3\ref*.75 feet long, 2.25 feet wide, and 2.25 feet high (114.3 centimeters long, 68.6 centimeters wide, and 68.6 centimeters high).\f* \v 11 \w Overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w it with pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w both inside|strong="H1004"\w* \w and out|strong="H2351"\w*, \w and make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w molding|strong="H2213"\w* \w around it|strong="H5439"\w*.
\p \v 12 \w Cast|strong="H3332"\w* \w four|strong="H702"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w rings|strong="H2885"\w* for it \w and fasten them|strong="H5414"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w its four|strong="H702"\w* \w feet|strong="H6471"\w*, \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w side|strong="H6763"\w* \w and two|strong="H8147"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the other|strong="H8145"\w*. \v 13 \w And make|strong="H6213"\w* \w poles|strong="H905"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w* \w and overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w*. \v 14 \w Insert|strong="H935"\w* \w the poles|strong="H905"\w* \w into the rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the sides|strong="H6763"\w* \w of the ark|strong="H727"\w*, \w in order to carry|strong="H5375"\w* \w it|strong="H727"\w*. \v 15 \w The poles|strong="H905"\w* \w are to remain|strong="H1961"\w* \w in the rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w of the ark|strong="H727"\w*; \w they must not|strong="H3808"\w* \w be removed|strong="H5493"\w*. \v 16 \w And place|strong="H5414"\w* \w inside|strong="H413"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*,\f + \fr 25:16 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments; also in verses 21 and 22.\f* \w which|strong="H834"\w* \w I will give|strong="H5414"\w* \w you|strong="H413"\w*.
\s1 The Mercy Seat
\r (\ref Exodus 37:6–9|EXO 37:6-9\ref*)
\p \v 17 \w And you are to construct|strong="H6213"\w* \w a mercy seat|strong="H3727"\w*\f + \fr 25:17 \ft Or \fqa an atonement cover\ft ; here and throughout Exodus\f* \w of pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w two|strong="H520"\w* \w and a half cubits|strong="H2677"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w* \w and a cubit|strong="H520"\w* \w and a half|strong="H2677"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*.\f + \fr 25:17 \ft The mercy seat was \ref approximately 3|3\ref*.75 feet long and 2.25 feet wide (114.3 centimeters long and 68.6 centimeters wide).\f* \v 18 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w cherubim|strong="H3742"\w* \w of hammered|strong="H4749"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w at the|strong="H8147"\w* \w ends|strong="H7098"\w* \w of the mercy seat|strong="H3727"\w*, \v 19 \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w cherub|strong="H3742"\w* \w on one|strong="H2088"\w* \w end|strong="H7098"\w* \w and one|strong="H259"\w* \w on the other|strong="H7098"\w*, \w all made|strong="H6213"\w* \w from one piece of gold|strong="H7098"\w*. \v 20 \w And the cherubim|strong="H3742"\w* \w are to have|strong="H1961"\w* \w wings|strong="H3671"\w* \w that spread|strong="H6566"\w* \w upward|strong="H4605"\w*, \w overshadowing|strong="H5526"\w* \w the mercy seat|strong="H3727"\w*. \w The cherubim are to face|strong="H6440"\w* \w each|strong="H376"\w* \w other|strong="H251"\w*, \w looking|strong="H1961"\w* \w toward|strong="H413"\w* \w the mercy seat|strong="H3727"\w*.
\p \v 21 \w Set|strong="H5414"\w* \w the mercy seat|strong="H3727"\w* \w atop|strong="H5921"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w and put|strong="H5414"\w* \w the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w I will give|strong="H5414"\w* \w you|strong="H413"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w*.
\p \v 22 \w And I will meet|strong="H3259"\w* with you \w there|strong="H8033"\w* \w above|strong="H5921"\w* \w the mercy seat|strong="H3727"\w*, \w between|strong="H996"\w* \w the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w cherubim|strong="H3742"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w are over|strong="H5921"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*;\f + \fr 25:22 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\f* \w I will speak|strong="H1696"\w* \w with you|strong="H854"\w* \w about all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w I command|strong="H6680"\w* \w you|strong="H853"\w* \w regarding|strong="H413"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*.
\s1 The Table of Showbread
\r (\ref Exodus 37:10–16|EXO 37:10-16\ref*; \ref Leviticus 24:5–9|LEV 24:5-9\ref*)
\p \v 23 \w You are also to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a table|strong="H7979"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w* \w two cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w*, \w a cubit|strong="H520"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*, \w and a cubit|strong="H520"\w* \w and a half|strong="H2677"\w* \w high|strong="H6967"\w*.\f + \fr 25:23 \ft The table was \ref approximately 3|3\ref* feet long, 1.5 feet wide, and 2.25 feet high (91.4 centimeters long, 45.7 centimeters wide, and 68.6 centimeters high).\f* \v 24 \w Overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w* \w with pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w and make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w molding|strong="H2213"\w* \w around it|strong="H5439"\w*. \v 25 \w And make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a rim|strong="H4526"\w* \w around it|strong="H5439"\w* \w a handbreadth wide|strong="H2948"\w*\f + \fr 25:25 \fqa A handbreadth\ft is \ref approximately 2|2\ref*.9 inches or 7.4 centimeters.\f* \w and put|strong="H6213"\w* \w a gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w molding|strong="H2213"\w* \w on|strong="H5439"\w* \w the rim|strong="H4526"\w*.
\p \v 26 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w four|strong="H702"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w rings|strong="H2885"\w* for the table \w and fasten|strong="H5414"\w* \w them|strong="H2885"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the four|strong="H702"\w* \w corners|strong="H6285"\w* \w at its four|strong="H702"\w* \w legs|strong="H7272"\w*. \v 27 \w The rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w are to be|strong="H1961"\w* \w close|strong="H5980"\w* \w to the rim|strong="H4526"\w*, \w to serve as holders|strong="H1004"\w* \w for the poles|strong="H905"\w* \w used to carry|strong="H5375"\w* \w the table|strong="H7979"\w*. \v 28 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w the poles|strong="H905"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w* \w and overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w so that the table|strong="H7979"\w* \w may be carried|strong="H5375"\w* with them.
\p \v 29 \w You are also to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w the plates|strong="H7086"\w* \w and dishes|strong="H3709"\w*, \w as well as the pitchers|strong="H7184"\w* \w and bowls|strong="H4518"\w* \w for pouring drink offerings|strong="H5258"\w*. \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w out of pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*.
\p \v 30 \w And place|strong="H5414"\w* \w the Bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w of the Presence|strong="H6440"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the table|strong="H7979"\w* \w before Me|strong="H6440"\w* \w at all times|strong="H8548"\w*.
\s1 The Lampstand
\r (\ref Exodus 37:17–24|EXO 37:17-24\ref*; \ref Numbers 8:1–4|NUM 8:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 31 \w Then you are to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a lampstand|strong="H4501"\w* \w of pure|strong="H2889"\w*, \w hammered|strong="H4749"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*. \w It|strong="H4501"\w* \w shall be made|strong="H6213"\w* \w of one piece|strong="H4480"\w*, \w including|strong="H1961"\w* \w its base|strong="H3409"\w* \w and shaft|strong="H7070"\w*, \w its cups|strong="H1375"\w*, \w and its buds|strong="H3730"\w* \w and petals|strong="H6525"\w*.
\p \v 32 \w Six|strong="H8337"\w* \w branches|strong="H7070"\w* \w are to extend|strong="H3318"\w* \w from the sides|strong="H6654"\w* \w of the lampstand|strong="H4501"\w* — \w three|strong="H7969"\w* \w on one|strong="H259"\w* \w side|strong="H6654"\w* \w and three|strong="H7969"\w* \w on the other|strong="H8145"\w*. \v 33 \w There are to be three|strong="H7969"\w* \w cups|strong="H1375"\w* \w shaped like almond blossoms|strong="H8246"\w* \w on the first|strong="H259"\w* \w branch|strong="H7070"\w*, \w each with buds|strong="H3730"\w* \w and petals|strong="H6525"\w*, \w three|strong="H7969"\w* \w on the next|strong="H259"\w* \w branch|strong="H7070"\w*, \w and the same|strong="H3651"\w* \w for all six|strong="H8337"\w* \w branches|strong="H7070"\w* \w that extend|strong="H3318"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the lampstand|strong="H4501"\w*.
\p \v 34 \w And on the lampstand|strong="H4501"\w* \w there shall be four|strong="H702"\w* \w cups|strong="H1375"\w* \w shaped like almond blossoms|strong="H8246"\w* \w with buds|strong="H3730"\w* \w and petals|strong="H6525"\w*. \v 35 \w For the six|strong="H8337"\w* \w branches|strong="H7070"\w* \w that extend|strong="H3318"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the lampstand|strong="H4501"\w*, \w a bud|strong="H3730"\w* \w must be under|strong="H8478"\w* \w the first pair|strong="H8147"\w* \w of branches|strong="H7070"\w*, \w a bud|strong="H3730"\w* \w under|strong="H8478"\w* \w the second pair|strong="H8147"\w*, \w and a bud|strong="H3730"\w* \w under|strong="H8478"\w* \w the third pair|strong="H8147"\w*. \v 36 \w The buds|strong="H3730"\w* \w and branches|strong="H7070"\w* \w are to be|strong="H1961"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w of one piece with the lampstand|strong="H259"\w*, \w hammered|strong="H4749"\w* \w out of pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*.
\p \v 37 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w lamps|strong="H5216"\w* \w and set them up|strong="H5927"\w* \w on the lampstand|strong="H853"\w* \w so that they|strong="H5216"\w* \w illuminate|strong="H215"\w* \w the area|strong="H5676"\w* \w in|strong="H5921"\w* \w front of it|strong="H6440"\w*. \v 38 \w The wick trimmers|strong="H4457"\w* \w and their trays|strong="H4289"\w* \w must be of pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*. \v 39 \w The lampstand|strong="H853"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w these|strong="H428"\w* \w utensils|strong="H3627"\w* \w shall be made|strong="H6213"\w* \w from|strong="H853"\w* \w a talent|strong="H3603"\w* \w of pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*.\f + \fr 25:39 \fqa A talent\ft is \ref approximately 75|75\ref*.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of gold.\f*
\p \v 40 \w See to it that|strong="H7200"\w* \w you make everything|strong="H6213"\w* \w according to the pattern|strong="H8403"\w* \w shown|strong="H7200"\w* \w you|strong="H859"\w* \w on the mountain|strong="H2022"\w*.\f + \fr 25:40 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 8:5|HEB 8:5\ref*\f*[’’]
\c 26
\s1 The Ten Curtains for the Tabernacle
\r (\ref Exodus 36:8–13|EXO 36:8-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 “\w You are to construct|strong="H6213"\w* \w the tabernacle itself|strong="H4908"\w* \w with ten|strong="H6235"\w* \w curtains|strong="H3407"\w* \w of finely spun|strong="H7806"\w* \w linen|strong="H8336"\w*, \w each with blue|strong="H8504"\w*, \w purple|strong="H713"\w*, \w and scarlet yarn|strong="H8438"\w*, \w and cherubim|strong="H3742"\w* \w skillfully|strong="H2803"\w* \w worked|strong="H4639"\w* \w into them|strong="H853"\w*. \v 2 \w Each|strong="H259"\w* \w curtain|strong="H3407"\w* \w shall be twenty-eight|strong="H8083"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w* \w and four|strong="H702"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*\f + \fr 26:2 \ft Each of the ten curtains was \ref approximately 42|42\ref* feet long and 6 feet wide (12.8 meters long and 1.8 meters wide).\f* — \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w curtains|strong="H3407"\w* \w the same|strong="H259"\w* \w size|strong="H4060"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w Five|strong="H2568"\w* \w of the curtains|strong="H3407"\w* \w are to be|strong="H1961"\w* \w joined|strong="H2266"\w* \w together|strong="H802"\w*, \w and the other five|strong="H2568"\w* \w joined|strong="H2266"\w* \w as well|strong="H802"\w*. \v 4 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w loops|strong="H3924"\w* \w of blue material|strong="H8504"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the edge|strong="H8193"\w* \w of the end|strong="H7098"\w* \w curtain|strong="H3407"\w* \w in the first|strong="H259"\w* \w set|strong="H2279"\w*, \w and do|strong="H6213"\w* \w the same|strong="H3651"\w* \w for the end|strong="H7020"\w* \w curtain|strong="H3407"\w* \w in the second|strong="H8145"\w* \w set|strong="H4225"\w*.
\p \v 5 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w loops|strong="H3924"\w* \w on one|strong="H259"\w* \w curtain|strong="H3407"\w* \w and fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w loops|strong="H3924"\w* \w on the end|strong="H7097"\w* \w curtain|strong="H3407"\w* \w of the second|strong="H8145"\w* \w set|strong="H4225"\w*, \w so that the loops|strong="H3924"\w* \w line up|strong="H6901"\w* \w opposite|strong="H802"\w* \w one another|strong="H269"\w*. \v 6 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w clasps as well|strong="H7165"\w*, \w and join|strong="H2266"\w* \w the curtains|strong="H3407"\w* \w together|strong="H802"\w* \w with the clasps|strong="H7165"\w*, \w so that the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w* \w will be|strong="H1961"\w* \w a unit|strong="H259"\w*.
\s1 The Eleven Curtains of Goat Hair
\r (\ref Exodus 36:14–19|EXO 36:14-19\ref*)
\p \v 7 \w You are to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w curtains|strong="H3407"\w* \w of goat hair|strong="H5795"\w* \w for the tent|strong="H168"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w* — \w eleven|strong="H6249"\w* \w curtains in all|strong="H3407"\w*. \v 8 \w Each|strong="H259"\w* \w of the eleven|strong="H6249"\w* \w curtains|strong="H3407"\w* \w is to be the same|strong="H259"\w* \w size|strong="H4060"\w* — \w thirty|strong="H7970"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w* \w and four|strong="H702"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*.\f + \fr 26:8 \ft Each of the eleven curtains was \ref approximately 45|45\ref* feet long and 6 feet wide (13.7 meters long and 1.8 meters wide).\f*
\p \v 9 \w Join|strong="H2266"\w* \w five|strong="H2568"\w* \w of the curtains|strong="H3407"\w* \w into one set|strong="H905"\w* \w and the other six|strong="H8337"\w* \w into another|strong="H3407"\w*. \w Then fold the sixth|strong="H8345"\w* \w curtain over|strong="H3407"\w* \w double|strong="H3717"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the front|strong="H4136"\w* \w of the tent|strong="H168"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w loops|strong="H3924"\w* \w along|strong="H5921"\w* \w the edge|strong="H8193"\w* \w of the|strong="H259"\w* \w end|strong="H7020"\w* \w curtain|strong="H3407"\w* \w in the first set|strong="H2279"\w*, \w and fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w loops|strong="H3924"\w* \w along|strong="H5921"\w* \w the edge|strong="H8193"\w* \w of the corresponding curtain|strong="H3407"\w* \w in the second|strong="H8145"\w* \w set|strong="H2279"\w*. \v 11 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w clasps|strong="H7165"\w* \w and put|strong="H935"\w* \w them|strong="H7165"\w* \w through the loops|strong="H3924"\w* \w to join|strong="H2266"\w* \w the tent|strong="H168"\w* \w together|strong="H1961"\w* \w as a unit|strong="H259"\w*.
\p \v 12 \w As for the overlap|strong="H5629"\w* \w that remains|strong="H5736"\w* \w of the tent|strong="H168"\w* \w curtains|strong="H3407"\w*, \w the half|strong="H2677"\w* \w curtain|strong="H3407"\w* \w that is left over|strong="H5736"\w* \w shall hang down|strong="H5628"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w the back|strong="H268"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*. \v 13 \w And the tent|strong="H168"\w* \w curtains will be|strong="H3407"\w* \w a cubit|strong="H520"\w*\f + \fr 26:13 \fqa A cubit\ft is \ref approximately 18|18\ref* inches or 45.7 centimeters.\f* \w longer|strong="H753"\w* \w on either side|strong="H2088"\w*, \w and the excess|strong="H5736"\w* \w will|strong="H1961"\w* \w hang|strong="H5628"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w the sides|strong="H6654"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w* \w to cover it|strong="H3680"\w*.
\p \v 14 \w Also make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a covering|strong="H4372"\w* \w for the tent|strong="H168"\w* \w out of ram|strong="H352"\w* \w skins|strong="H5785"\w* \w dyed red|strong="H119"\w*, \w and over that|strong="H4605"\w* \w a covering|strong="H4372"\w* \w of fine leather|strong="H8476"\w*.\f + \fr 26:14 \ft Possibly the hides of large aquatic mammals\f*
\s1 The Frames and Bases
\r (\ref Exodus 36:20–34|EXO 36:20-34\ref*)
\p \v 15 \w You are to construct|strong="H6213"\w* \w upright|strong="H5975"\w* \w frames|strong="H7175"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w* \w for the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*. \v 16 \w Each frame|strong="H7175"\w* \w is to be ten|strong="H6235"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w* \w and a cubit|strong="H520"\w* \w and a half|strong="H2677"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*.\f + \fr 26:16 \ft Each frame was \ref approximately 15|15\ref* feet long and 2.25 feet wide (4.6 meters long and 68.6 centimeters wide).\f* \v 17 \w Two|strong="H8147"\w* \w tenons|strong="H3027"\w*\f + \fr 26:17 \ft That is, projecting pieces of wood made for insertion into another piece; similarly in verse 19.\f* \w must be connected|strong="H7947"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w each|strong="H802"\w* \w other|strong="H269"\w* \w for each|strong="H259"\w* \w frame|strong="H7175"\w*. \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the frames|strong="H7175"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w* \w in this way|strong="H3651"\w*.
\p \v 18 \w Construct|strong="H6213"\w* \w twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w frames|strong="H7175"\w* \w for the south|strong="H5045"\w* \w side|strong="H6285"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*, \v 19 \w with|strong="H6213"\w* \w forty|strong="H705"\w* \w silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w* \w under|strong="H8478"\w* \w the twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w frames|strong="H7175"\w* — \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w* \w for each|strong="H259"\w* \w frame|strong="H7175"\w*, \w one under each|strong="H8147"\w* \w tenon|strong="H3027"\w*.
\p \v 20 \w For the second|strong="H8145"\w* \w side|strong="H6763"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*, \w the north|strong="H6828"\w* \w side|strong="H6285"\w*, \w make twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w frames|strong="H7175"\w* \v 21 \w and forty|strong="H705"\w* \w silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w* — \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w* \w under|strong="H8478"\w* \w each|strong="H259"\w* \w frame|strong="H7175"\w*.
\p \v 22 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w six|strong="H8337"\w* \w frames|strong="H7175"\w* \w for the rear|strong="H3411"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*, \w the west side|strong="H3220"\w*, \v 23 \w and|strong="H6213"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w frames|strong="H7175"\w* \w for the two back|strong="H3411"\w* \w corners|strong="H4742"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*, \v 24 \w coupled|strong="H8380"\w* \w together|strong="H3162"\w* \w from|strong="H5921"\w* \w bottom|strong="H4295"\w* \w to top|strong="H7218"\w* \w and fitted into|strong="H413"\w* \w a single|strong="H259"\w* \w ring|strong="H2885"\w*. \w These|strong="H8147"\w* \w will serve as|strong="H1961"\w* \w the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w corners|strong="H4740"\w*. \v 25 \w So there are to be|strong="H1961"\w* \w eight|strong="H8083"\w* \w frames|strong="H7175"\w* \w and sixteen|strong="H8337"\w* \w silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w* — \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w under|strong="H8478"\w* \w each|strong="H259"\w* \w frame|strong="H7175"\w*.
\p \v 26 \w You are also to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w five|strong="H2568"\w* \w crossbars|strong="H1280"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w* \w for the frames|strong="H7175"\w* \w on one|strong="H259"\w* \w side|strong="H6763"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*, \v 27 \w five|strong="H2568"\w* \w for those|strong="H7175"\w* \w on the other|strong="H8145"\w* \w side|strong="H6763"\w*, \w and five|strong="H2568"\w* \w for those|strong="H7175"\w* \w on the rear|strong="H3411"\w* \w side|strong="H6763"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*, \w to the west|strong="H3220"\w*.
\p \v 28 \w The central|strong="H8484"\w* \w crossbar|strong="H1280"\w* \w in the middle|strong="H8432"\w* \w of the frames|strong="H7175"\w* \w shall extend|strong="H1272"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w one end|strong="H7097"\w* \w to the other|strong="H413"\w*. \v 29 \w Overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w the frames|strong="H7175"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w and make|strong="H6213"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w to hold|strong="H1004"\w* \w the crossbars|strong="H1280"\w*. \w Also overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w the crossbars|strong="H1280"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w*.
\p \v 30 \w So you are to set up|strong="H6965"\w* \w the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w* \w according to the pattern|strong="H4941"\w* \w shown you|strong="H7200"\w* \w on the mountain|strong="H2022"\w*.
\s1 The Veil
\r (\ref Exodus 36:35–36|EXO 36:35-36\ref*)
\p \v 31 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a veil|strong="H6532"\w* \w of blue|strong="H8504"\w*, \w purple|strong="H713"\w*, \w and scarlet yarn|strong="H8438"\w*, \w and finely spun|strong="H7806"\w* \w linen|strong="H8336"\w*, \w with cherubim|strong="H3742"\w* \w skillfully|strong="H2803"\w* \w worked|strong="H4639"\w* \w into it|strong="H6213"\w*. \v 32 \w Hang|strong="H5414"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w hooks|strong="H2053"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w four|strong="H702"\w* \w posts|strong="H5982"\w* \w of acacia wood|strong="H7848"\w*, \w overlaid|strong="H6823"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w and standing on|strong="H5921"\w* \w four|strong="H702"\w* \w silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w*. \v 33 \w And hang|strong="H5414"\w* \w the veil|strong="H6532"\w* \w from|strong="H8478"\w* \w the clasps|strong="H7165"\w* \w and place|strong="H935"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*\f + \fr 26:33 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\ft ; also in verse 34\f* \w behind|strong="H1004"\w* \w the veil|strong="H6532"\w*. \w So the veil|strong="H6532"\w* \w will separate|strong="H914"\w* \w the Holy Place|strong="H6944"\w* \w from the Most Holy Place|strong="H6944"\w*.\f + \fr 26:33 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies\ft ; also in verse 34\f*
\p \v 34 \w Put|strong="H5414"\w* \w the mercy seat|strong="H3727"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w* \w in the Most Holy Place|strong="H6944"\w*. \v 35 \w And place|strong="H7760"\w* \w the table|strong="H7979"\w* \w outside|strong="H2351"\w* \w the veil|strong="H6532"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the north|strong="H6828"\w* \w side|strong="H6763"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*, \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w put|strong="H5414"\w* \w the lampstand|strong="H4501"\w* \w opposite|strong="H5227"\w* \w the table|strong="H7979"\w*, \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the south|strong="H8486"\w* \w side|strong="H6763"\w*.
\s1 The Curtain for the Entrance
\r (\ref Exodus 36:37–38|EXO 36:37-38\ref*)
\p \v 36 \w For the entrance|strong="H6607"\w* \w to the tent|strong="H168"\w*, \w you are to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a curtain|strong="H4539"\w* \w embroidered|strong="H7551"\w* \w with blue|strong="H8504"\w*, \w purple|strong="H713"\w*, \w and scarlet yarn|strong="H8438"\w*, \w and finely spun|strong="H7806"\w* \w linen|strong="H8336"\w*. \v 37 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w five|strong="H2568"\w* \w posts|strong="H5982"\w* \w of acacia wood|strong="H7848"\w* \w for the curtain|strong="H4539"\w*, \w overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w hooks|strong="H2053"\w*, \w and cast|strong="H3332"\w* \w five|strong="H2568"\w* \w bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w* for them.[’’]
\c 27
\s1 The Bronze Altar
\r (\ref Exodus 38:1–7|EXO 38:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 “\w You are to build|strong="H6213"\w* \w an altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w*. \w The altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w must be|strong="H1961"\w* \w square|strong="H7251"\w*, \w five|strong="H2568"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w*, \w five|strong="H2568"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*, \w and three|strong="H7969"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w high|strong="H6967"\w*.\f + \fr 27:1 \ft The altar was \ref approximately 7|7\ref*.5 feet in length and width, and 4.5 feet high (2.3 meters in length and width, and 1.4 meters high).\f* \v 2 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a horn|strong="H7161"\w* \w on each of|strong="H5921"\w* \w its four|strong="H702"\w* \w corners|strong="H6438"\w*, \w so that the horns|strong="H7161"\w* \w are|strong="H1961"\w* \w of one piece|strong="H4480"\w*, \w and overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w it with bronze|strong="H5178"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w its utensils|strong="H3627"\w* \w of bronze|strong="H5178"\w* — \w its pots|strong="H5518"\w* \w for removing ashes|strong="H1878"\w*, \w its shovels|strong="H3257"\w*, \w its sprinkling bowls|strong="H4219"\w*, \w its meat forks|strong="H4207"\w*, \w and its firepans|strong="H4289"\w*. \v 4 \w Construct|strong="H6213"\w* for it \w a grate|strong="H4345"\w* \w of bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w mesh|strong="H7568"\w*, \w and make a|strong="H6213"\w* \w bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w ring|strong="H2885"\w* \w at|strong="H5921"\w* \w each of the four|strong="H702"\w* \w corners|strong="H7098"\w* \w of|strong="H5921"\w* \w the mesh|strong="H7568"\w*. \v 5 \w Set|strong="H5414"\w* \w the grate|strong="H853"\w* \w beneath|strong="H4295"\w* \w the ledge|strong="H3749"\w* \w of the altar|strong="H4196"\w*, \w so that the mesh|strong="H7568"\w* \w comes|strong="H1961"\w* \w halfway|strong="H2677"\w* \w up|strong="H5704"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w*.
\p \v 6 \w Additionally, make|strong="H6213"\w* \w poles|strong="H905"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w* \w for the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w and overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w with bronze|strong="H5178"\w*. \v 7 \w The poles|strong="H905"\w* \w are to be inserted|strong="H935"\w* \w into the rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w so that the poles|strong="H905"\w* \w are|strong="H1961"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w sides|strong="H6763"\w* \w of the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w when it is carried|strong="H5375"\w*.
\p \v 8 \w Construct|strong="H6213"\w* \w the altar|strong="H853"\w* \w with boards|strong="H3871"\w* \w so that it is hollow|strong="H5014"\w*. \w It is to be made|strong="H6213"\w* \w just as|strong="H834"\w* \w you were shown|strong="H7200"\w* \w on the mountain|strong="H2022"\w*.
\s1 The Courtyard
\r (\ref Exodus 38:9–20|EXO 38:9-20\ref*)
\p \v 9 \w You are also to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w for the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w*. \w On the south|strong="H5045"\w* \w side|strong="H6285"\w* \w of the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w make curtains|strong="H7050"\w* \w of finely spun|strong="H7806"\w* \w linen|strong="H8336"\w*, \w a hundred|strong="H3967"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w*\f + \fr 27:9 \fqa \ref 100|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 150|150\ref* feet or 45.7 meters; also in verse 11.\f* \w on one|strong="H259"\w* \w side|strong="H6285"\w*, \v 10 \w with twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w posts|strong="H5982"\w* \w and twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w*, \w and silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w hooks|strong="H2053"\w* \w and bands|strong="H2838"\w* \w on the posts|strong="H5982"\w*.
\p \v 11 \w Likewise|strong="H3651"\w* \w there are to be curtains|strong="H7050"\w* \w on the north|strong="H6828"\w* \w side|strong="H6285"\w*, \w a hundred|strong="H3967"\w* \w cubits|strong="H753"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w*, \w with twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w posts|strong="H5982"\w* \w and twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w*, \w and with silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w hooks|strong="H2053"\w* \w and bands|strong="H2838"\w* \w on the posts|strong="H5982"\w*. \v 12 \w The curtains|strong="H7050"\w* \w on the west|strong="H3220"\w* \w side|strong="H6285"\w* \w of the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w shall be fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*,\f + \fr 27:12 \fqa \ref 50|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 75|75\ref* feet or 22.9 meters; also in verse 13.\f* \w with ten|strong="H6235"\w* \w posts|strong="H5982"\w* \w and ten|strong="H6235"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w*.
\p \v 13 \w The east|strong="H6924"\w* \w side|strong="H6285"\w* \w of the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w*, \w toward the sunrise|strong="H4217"\w*, \w is to be fifty|strong="H2572"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*. \v 14 \w Make the curtains|strong="H7050"\w* \w on one side|strong="H3802"\w* \w fifteen|strong="H2568"\w* \w cubits long|strong="H520"\w*,\f + \fr 27:14 \fqa \ref 15|5\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 22|22\ref*.5 feet or 6.9 meters; also in verse 15.\f* \w with three|strong="H7969"\w* \w posts|strong="H5982"\w* \w and three|strong="H7969"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w*, \v 15 \w and the curtains|strong="H7050"\w* \w on the other|strong="H8145"\w* \w side|strong="H3802"\w* \w fifteen cubits long|strong="H2568"\w*, \w with three|strong="H7969"\w* \w posts|strong="H5982"\w* \w and three|strong="H7969"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w*.
\p \v 16 \w The gate|strong="H8179"\w* \w of the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w shall be twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w cubits long|strong="H520"\w*,\f + \fr 27:16 \fqa \ref 20|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 30|30\ref* feet or 9.1 meters.\f* \w with a curtain|strong="H4539"\w* \w embroidered|strong="H7551"\w* \w with blue|strong="H8504"\w*, \w purple|strong="H713"\w*, \w and scarlet yarn|strong="H8438"\w*, \w and finely spun|strong="H7806"\w* \w linen|strong="H8336"\w*. \w It shall have four|strong="H702"\w* \w posts|strong="H5982"\w* \w and four|strong="H702"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w*.
\p \v 17 \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w the posts|strong="H5982"\w* \w around|strong="H5439"\w* \w the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w shall have silver bands|strong="H2836"\w*, \w silver|strong="H3701"\w* \w hooks|strong="H2053"\w*, \w and bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w*. \v 18 \w The entire|strong="H2572"\w* \w courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w shall be a hundred|strong="H3967"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w* \w and fifty cubits|strong="H2572"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*,\f + \fr 27:18 \ft The courtyard was \ref approximately 150|150\ref* feet long and 75 feet wide (45.7 meters long and 22.9 meters wide).\f* \w with curtains of finely spun|strong="H7806"\w* \w linen|strong="H8336"\w* \w five|strong="H2568"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w high|strong="H6967"\w*,\f + \fr 27:18 \fqa 5 cubits\ft is \ref approximately 7|7\ref*.5 feet or 2.3 meters.\f* \w and with bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w bases|strong="H134"\w*. \v 19 \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w the utensils|strong="H3627"\w* \w of the tabernacle|strong="H4908"\w* \w for every|strong="H3605"\w* \w use|strong="H5656"\w*, \w including all|strong="H3605"\w* \w its tent pegs|strong="H3489"\w* \w and|strong="H3605"\w* \w the tent pegs|strong="H3489"\w* \w of the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w*, \w shall be made of bronze|strong="H5178"\w*.
\s1 The Oil for the Lamps
\r (\ref Leviticus 24:1–4|LEV 24:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 20 \w And you|strong="H859"\w* \w are to command|strong="H6680"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w to bring|strong="H3947"\w* \w you|strong="H413"\w* \w pure|strong="H2134"\w* \w oil|strong="H8081"\w* \w of pressed|strong="H3795"\w* \w olives|strong="H2132"\w* \w for the light|strong="H3974"\w*, \w to keep the lamps|strong="H5216"\w* \w burning|strong="H5927"\w* \w continually|strong="H8548"\w*.
\p \v 21 \w In the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w*, \w outside|strong="H2351"\w* \w the veil|strong="H6532"\w* \w that is|strong="H834"\w* \w in front of|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*,\f + \fr 27:21 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments.\f* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w are to tend|strong="H6186"\w* \w the lamps|strong="H853"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w from evening|strong="H6153"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w morning|strong="H1242"\w*. \w This is to be a permanent|strong="H5769"\w* \w statute|strong="H2708"\w* \w for the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*.[’’]
\c 28
\s1 Garments for the Priests
\p \v 1 “\w Next|strong="H859"\w*, \w have your brother|strong="H251"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w brought|strong="H7126"\w* \w to you|strong="H413"\w* \w from among|strong="H8432"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w along with|strong="H854"\w* \w his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w Nadab|strong="H5070"\w*, \w Abihu|strong="H30"\w*, \w Eleazar|strong="H499"\w*, \w and Ithamar|strong="H385"\w*, \w to serve Me as priests|strong="H3547"\w*. \v 2 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w garments|strong="H899"\w* \w for your brother|strong="H251"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w*, \w to give him glory|strong="H3519"\w* \w and splendor|strong="H8597"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w You|strong="H859"\w* \w are to instruct|strong="H1696"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the skilled craftsmen|strong="H2450"\w*, \w whom|strong="H834"\w* \w I have filled|strong="H4390"\w* \w with a spirit|strong="H7307"\w* \w of wisdom|strong="H2451"\w*, \w to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w garments|strong="H899"\w* \w for Aaron’s|strong="H175"\w* \w consecration|strong="H6942"\w*, \w so that he may serve Me as priest|strong="H3547"\w*. \v 4 \w These|strong="H428"\w* \w are the garments|strong="H899"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w they shall make|strong="H6213"\w*: \w a breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w*, \w an ephod|strong="H646"\w*, \w a robe|strong="H4598"\w*, \w a woven|strong="H8665"\w* \w tunic|strong="H3801"\w*, \w a turban|strong="H4701"\w*, \w and a sash|strong="H73"\w*. \w They are to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w these holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w garments|strong="H899"\w* \w for your brother|strong="H251"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w*, \w so that they may serve Me as priests|strong="H3547"\w*. \v 5 \w They|strong="H1992"\w* \w shall use|strong="H3947"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w along with|strong="H853"\w* \w blue|strong="H8504"\w*, \w purple|strong="H713"\w*, \w and scarlet yarn|strong="H8438"\w*, \w and fine linen|strong="H8336"\w*.
\s1 The Ephod
\r (\ref Exodus 39:1–7|EXO 39:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 6 \w They are to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w the ephod|strong="H646"\w* \w of finely spun|strong="H7806"\w* \w linen|strong="H8336"\w* \w embroidered|strong="H4639"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w and with blue|strong="H8504"\w*, \w purple|strong="H713"\w*, \w and scarlet yarn|strong="H8438"\w*. \v 7 \w It shall have|strong="H1961"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w shoulder pieces|strong="H3802"\w* \w attached|strong="H2266"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w of its corners|strong="H7098"\w*, \w so it can be fastened|strong="H2266"\w*. \v 8 \w And the skillfully woven waistband|strong="H2805"\w* \w of|strong="H5921"\w* \w the ephod|strong="H642"\w* \w must be|strong="H1961"\w* \w of one piece|strong="H4480"\w*, \w of the same workmanship|strong="H4639"\w* — \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w with blue|strong="H8504"\w*, \w purple|strong="H713"\w*, \w and scarlet yarn|strong="H8438"\w*, \w and with finely spun|strong="H7806"\w* \w linen|strong="H8336"\w*.
\p \v 9 \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w onyx|strong="H7718"\w* \w stones|strong="H68"\w* \w and engrave|strong="H6605"\w* \w on them|strong="H5921"\w* \w the names|strong="H8034"\w* \w of the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*: \v 10 \w six|strong="H8337"\w* \w of their names|strong="H8034"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w stone|strong="H68"\w* \w and the remaining|strong="H3498"\w* \w six|strong="H8337"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the other|strong="H8145"\w*, \w in the order of their birth|strong="H8435"\w*. \v 11 \w Engrave|strong="H6605"\w* \w the names|strong="H8034"\w* \w of the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w on the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w stones|strong="H68"\w* \w the way a gem|strong="H68"\w* \w cutter|strong="H2796"\w* \w engraves|strong="H6603"\w* \w a seal|strong="H2368"\w*. \w Then mount|strong="H5437"\w* \w the stones|strong="H853"\w* \w in gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w filigree settings|strong="H4865"\w*. \v 12 \w Fasten|strong="H7760"\w* \w both|strong="H8147"\w* \w stones|strong="H68"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the shoulder pieces|strong="H3802"\w* \w of the ephod|strong="H646"\w* \w as memorial|strong="H2146"\w* \w stones|strong="H68"\w* \w for the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w is to bear|strong="H5375"\w* \w their names|strong="H8034"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w his two|strong="H8147"\w* \w shoulders|strong="H3802"\w* \w as a memorial|strong="H2146"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 13 \w Fashion|strong="H6213"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w filigree settings|strong="H4865"\w* \v 14 \w and two|strong="H8147"\w* \w chains|strong="H8333"\w* \w of pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w made|strong="H6213"\w* \w of braided|strong="H4020"\w* \w cord|strong="H5688"\w* \w work|strong="H4639"\w*; \w and attach|strong="H5414"\w* \w these|strong="H5688"\w* \w chains|strong="H8333"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the settings|strong="H4865"\w*.
\s1 The Breastpiece
\r (\ref Exodus 39:8–21|EXO 39:8-21\ref*)
\p \v 15 \w You are also to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w* \w of judgment|strong="H4941"\w* \w with the same workmanship|strong="H4639"\w* \w as the ephod|strong="H646"\w*. \w Construct|strong="H6213"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w with blue|strong="H8504"\w*, \w purple|strong="H713"\w*, \w and scarlet yarn|strong="H8438"\w*, \w and with finely spun|strong="H7806"\w* \w linen|strong="H8336"\w*. \v 16 \w It must be|strong="H1961"\w* \w square|strong="H7251"\w* \w when folded over double|strong="H3717"\w*, \w a span|strong="H2239"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w* \w and a span|strong="H2239"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*.\f + \fr 28:16 \ft The breastpiece, when folded over, was \ref approximately 9|9\ref* inches or 22.9 centimeters in both length and width.\f*
\p \v 17 \w And mount|strong="H4390"\w* on it \w a setting|strong="H4396"\w* \w of gemstones|strong="H68"\w*, \w four|strong="H702"\w* \w rows|strong="H2905"\w* \w of stones|strong="H68"\w*:\f + \fr 28:17 \ft The precise identification of some of these gemstones is uncertain.\f*
\li1 \w In the first|strong="H259"\w* \w row there shall be|strong="H2905"\w* \w a ruby|strong="H124"\w*, \w a topaz|strong="H6357"\w*, \w and an emerald|strong="H1304"\w*;
\li1 \v 18 \w in the second|strong="H8145"\w* \w row|strong="H2905"\w* \w a turquoise|strong="H5306"\w*, \w a sapphire|strong="H5601"\w*, \w and a diamond|strong="H3095"\w*;
\li1 \v 19 \w in the third|strong="H7992"\w* \w row|strong="H2905"\w* \w a jacinth|strong="H3958"\w*, \w an agate|strong="H7618"\w*, \w and an amethyst|strong="H306"\w*;
\li1 \v 20 \w and in the fourth|strong="H7243"\w* \w row|strong="H2905"\w* \w a beryl|strong="H8658"\w*, \w an onyx|strong="H7718"\w*, \w and a jasper|strong="H3471"\w*.
\p \w Mount these stones|strong="H1961"\w* \w in gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w filigree settings|strong="H4396"\w*. \v 21 \w The twelve|strong="H8147"\w* \w stones|strong="H68"\w* \w are|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w correspond to the names|strong="H8034"\w* \w of the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w each|strong="H376"\w* \w engraved|strong="H6603"\w* \w like a seal|strong="H2368"\w* \w with|strong="H5921"\w* \w the name|strong="H8034"\w* \w of one of the twelve|strong="H8147"\w* \w tribes|strong="H7626"\w*.
\p \v 22 \w For the breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w*, \w make|strong="H6213"\w* \w braided chains|strong="H1383"\w* \w like cords|strong="H4639"\w* \w of pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*. \v 23 \w You are also to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w and fasten|strong="H5414"\w* \w them|strong="H8147"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w corners|strong="H7098"\w* \w of the breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w*. \v 24 \w Then fasten|strong="H5414"\w* \w the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w chains|strong="H5688"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w gold rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the corners|strong="H7098"\w* \w of the breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w*, \v 25 \w and fasten|strong="H5414"\w* \w the other|strong="H8147"\w* \w ends|strong="H7098"\w* \w of the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w chains|strong="H5688"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w filigree settings|strong="H4865"\w*, \w attaching them|strong="H5414"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the shoulder pieces|strong="H3802"\w* \w of the ephod|strong="H646"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the front|strong="H4136"\w*.
\p \v 26 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w two more|strong="H8147"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w and attach|strong="H7760"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the other two|strong="H8147"\w* \w corners|strong="H7098"\w* \w of the breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w*, \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the inside|strong="H1004"\w* \w edge|strong="H8193"\w* \w next to|strong="H413"\w* \w the ephod|strong="H646"\w*.
\p \v 27 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w two additional|strong="H8147"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w and attach|strong="H5414"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the bottom|strong="H4295"\w* \w of the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w shoulder pieces|strong="H3802"\w* \w of the ephod|strong="H646"\w*, \w on its front|strong="H4136"\w*, \w near|strong="H5980"\w* \w its seam|strong="H4225"\w* \w just above|strong="H4605"\w* \w its woven waistband|strong="H2805"\w*. \v 28 \w The rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w of the breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w* \w shall be tied|strong="H7405"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w of the ephod|strong="H646"\w* \w with a cord|strong="H6616"\w* \w of blue yarn|strong="H8504"\w*, \w so that the breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w* \w is|strong="H1961"\w* \w above|strong="H5921"\w* \w the waistband|strong="H2805"\w* \w of the ephod|strong="H646"\w* \w and does not|strong="H3808"\w* \w swing out|strong="H2118"\w* \w from|strong="H5921"\w* \w the ephod|strong="H646"\w*.
\p \v 29 \w Whenever Aaron enters|strong="H935"\w* \w the Holy Place|strong="H6944"\w*, \w he|strong="H175"\w* \w shall bear|strong="H5375"\w* \w the names|strong="H8034"\w* \w of the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w his heart|strong="H3820"\w* \w on the breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w* \w of judgment|strong="H4941"\w*, \w as a continual|strong="H8548"\w* \w reminder|strong="H2146"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 30 \w And place|strong="H5414"\w* \w the Urim|strong="H224"\w* \w and Thummim|strong="H8550"\w*\f + \fr 28:30 \ft Literally \fqa Lights and Perfections\f* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w the breastpiece|strong="H2833"\w* \w of judgment|strong="H4941"\w*, \w so that they will also be|strong="H1961"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w Aaron’s|strong="H175"\w* \w heart|strong="H3820"\w* \w whenever he comes|strong="H935"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w will continually|strong="H8548"\w* \w carry|strong="H5375"\w* \w the judgment|strong="H4941"\w* \w of the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w his heart|strong="H3820"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\s1 Additional Priestly Garments
\r (\ref Exodus 39:22–31|EXO 39:22-31\ref*)
\p \v 31 \w You are to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w the robe|strong="H4598"\w* \w of the ephod|strong="H646"\w* \w entirely|strong="H3632"\w* \w of blue cloth|strong="H8504"\w*, \v 32 \w with|strong="H1961"\w* \w an opening|strong="H6310"\w* \w at its top|strong="H7218"\w* \w in the center|strong="H8432"\w*. \w Around the opening|strong="H5439"\w* \w shall be|strong="H1961"\w* \w a woven|strong="H4639"\w* \w collar|strong="H8193"\w* \w with an opening|strong="H6310"\w* \w like that|strong="H6310"\w* \w of a garment|strong="H8473"\w*,\f + \fr 28:32 \ft The meaning of the Hebrew word is uncertain; possibly \fqa a coat of mail\ft .\f* \w so that|strong="H1961"\w* it \w will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w tear|strong="H7167"\w*.
\p \v 33 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w pomegranates|strong="H7416"\w* \w of blue|strong="H8504"\w*, \w purple|strong="H713"\w*, \w and scarlet yarn|strong="H8438"\w* \w all the way around the lower|strong="H5439"\w* \w hem|strong="H7757"\w*, \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w bells|strong="H6472"\w* \w between|strong="H8432"\w* \w them|strong="H5439"\w*, \v 34 \w alternating|strong="H5439"\w* \w the gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w bells|strong="H6472"\w* \w and pomegranates|strong="H7416"\w* \w around the lower hem|strong="H7757"\w* \w of the robe|strong="H4598"\w*.
\p \v 35 \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w must wear the robe|strong="H5921"\w* \w whenever he ministers|strong="H8334"\w*, \w and its sound|strong="H6963"\w* \w will be heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w when he enters|strong="H935"\w* \w or exits|strong="H3318"\w* \w the sanctuary|strong="H6944"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w so that he will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w die|strong="H4191"\w*.
\p \v 36 \w You are to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a plate|strong="H6731"\w* \w of pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w and engrave|strong="H6605"\w* \w on it|strong="H5921"\w* \w as|strong="H6603"\w* \w on a seal|strong="H2368"\w*:
\pc \w HOLY|strong="H6944"\w* \w TO THE LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.\f + \fr 28:36 \ft That is, \fqa the LORD\f*
\p \v 37 \w Fasten|strong="H7760"\w* \w to it|strong="H5921"\w* \w a blue|strong="H8504"\w* \w cord|strong="H6616"\w* \w to mount it on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the turban|strong="H4701"\w*; \w it shall be|strong="H1961"\w* \w on|strong="H413"\w* \w the front|strong="H4136"\w* \w of the turban|strong="H4701"\w*. \v 38 \w And it will be worn|strong="H1961"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w Aaron’s|strong="H175"\w* \w forehead|strong="H4696"\w*, \w so that he|strong="H175"\w* \w may bear|strong="H5375"\w* \w the iniquity|strong="H5771"\w* \w of the holy things|strong="H6944"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w with regard to all|strong="H3605"\w* \w their holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w gifts|strong="H4979"\w*. \w It shall always|strong="H8548"\w* \w be|strong="H1961"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w his forehead|strong="H4696"\w*, \w so that they may be acceptable|strong="H7522"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 39 \w You are to weave|strong="H7660"\w* \w the tunic|strong="H3801"\w* \w with fine linen|strong="H8336"\w*, \w make|strong="H6213"\w* \w the turban|strong="H4701"\w* \w of fine linen|strong="H8336"\w*, \w and fashion|strong="H6213"\w* \w an embroidered|strong="H7551"\w* \w sash|strong="H73"\w*. \v 40 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w tunics|strong="H3801"\w*, \w sashes|strong="H73"\w*, \w and headbands|strong="H4021"\w* \w for Aaron’s|strong="H175"\w* \w sons|strong="H1121"\w*, \w to give|strong="H6213"\w* them \w glory|strong="H3519"\w* \w and splendor|strong="H8597"\w*.
\p \v 41 \w After you put|strong="H3847"\w* \w these garments|strong="H853"\w* \w on your brother|strong="H251"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w*, \w anoint|strong="H4886"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w*, \w ordain|strong="H4390"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w*, \w and consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w so that they may serve Me as priests|strong="H3547"\w*.
\p \v 42 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w linen|strong="H906"\w* \w undergarments|strong="H4370"\w* \w to cover|strong="H3680"\w* their \w bare|strong="H6172"\w* \w flesh|strong="H1320"\w*, \w extending|strong="H1961"\w* \w from waist|strong="H4975"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w thigh|strong="H3409"\w*. \v 43 \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w must wear them|strong="H1961"\w* \w whenever they enter|strong="H935"\w* \w the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w approach|strong="H5066"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w to minister|strong="H8334"\w* \w in the Holy Place|strong="H6944"\w*, \w so that they will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w incur|strong="H5375"\w* \w guilt|strong="H5771"\w* \w and die|strong="H4191"\w*. \w This is to be a permanent|strong="H5769"\w* \w statute|strong="H2708"\w* \w for Aaron|strong="H310"\w* \w and his descendants|strong="H2233"\w*.[’’]
\c 29
\s1 Consecration of the Priests
\r (\ref Leviticus 8:1–13|LEV 8:1-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 “\w Now this|strong="H2088"\w* \w is what|strong="H834"\w* \w you are to do|strong="H6213"\w* \w to consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w Aaron and his sons|strong="H853"\w* \w to serve Me as priests|strong="H3547"\w*: \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w a|strong="H259"\w* \w young|strong="H1121"\w* \w bull|strong="H6499"\w* \w and two|strong="H8147"\w* \w rams|strong="H352"\w* \w without blemish|strong="H8549"\w*, \v 2 \w along with unleavened|strong="H4682"\w* \w bread|strong="H3899"\w*, \w unleavened|strong="H4682"\w* \w cakes|strong="H2471"\w* \w mixed|strong="H1101"\w* \w with oil|strong="H8081"\w*, \w and unleavened|strong="H4682"\w* \w wafers|strong="H7550"\w* \w anointed|strong="H4886"\w* \w with oil|strong="H8081"\w*. \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w out of fine wheat|strong="H2406"\w* \w flour|strong="H5560"\w*, \v 3 \w put|strong="H5414"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w in|strong="H5921"\w* \w a|strong="H259"\w* \w basket|strong="H5536"\w*, \w and present|strong="H7126"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w in the basket|strong="H5536"\w*, \w along with the bull|strong="H6499"\w* \w and the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w rams|strong="H352"\w*.
\p \v 4 \w Then|strong="H853"\w* \w present|strong="H7126"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the entrance|strong="H6607"\w* \w to the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w* \w and wash|strong="H7364"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w with water|strong="H4325"\w*. \v 5 \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w the garments|strong="H899"\w* \w and clothe|strong="H3847"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w with the tunic|strong="H3801"\w*, \w the robe|strong="H4598"\w* \w of the ephod|strong="H646"\w*, \w the ephod itself|strong="H646"\w*, \w and the breastplate|strong="H2833"\w*. \w Fasten|strong="H640"\w* \w the ephod|strong="H646"\w* on him \w with its woven waistband|strong="H2805"\w*. \v 6 \w Put|strong="H7760"\w* \w the turban|strong="H4701"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w his head|strong="H7218"\w* \w and attach|strong="H5414"\w* \w the holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w diadem|strong="H5145"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the turban|strong="H4701"\w*. \v 7 \w Then take|strong="H3947"\w* \w the anointing|strong="H4888"\w* \w oil|strong="H8081"\w* \w and anoint him|strong="H4886"\w* \w by pouring|strong="H3332"\w* \w it on|strong="H5921"\w* \w his head|strong="H7218"\w*.
\p \v 8 \w Present|strong="H7126"\w* \w his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w as well|strong="H853"\w* \w and clothe them|strong="H3847"\w* \w with tunics|strong="H3801"\w*. \v 9 \w Wrap|strong="H2296"\w* \w the sashes|strong="H73"\w* \w around Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w and tie|strong="H2280"\w* \w headbands|strong="H4021"\w* on them. \w The priesthood|strong="H3550"\w* \w shall be|strong="H1961"\w* theirs \w by a permanent|strong="H5769"\w* \w statute|strong="H2708"\w*. \w In this way you are to ordain|strong="H4390"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w*.
\s1 The Order of the Sacrifices
\r (\ref Leviticus 8:22–36|LEV 8:22-36\ref*)
\p \v 10 \w You are to present|strong="H7126"\w* \w the bull|strong="H6499"\w* \w at the front|strong="H6440"\w* \w of the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w*, \w and Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w are to lay|strong="H5564"\w* \w their hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w its|strong="H6499"\w* \w head|strong="H7218"\w*. \v 11 \w And you shall slaughter|strong="H7819"\w* \w the bull|strong="H6499"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w at the entrance|strong="H6607"\w* \w to the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w*. \v 12 \w Take some|strong="H3947"\w* \w of the blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w of the bull|strong="H6499"\w* \w and put|strong="H5414"\w* \w it on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the horns|strong="H7161"\w* \w of the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w with your finger|strong="H676"\w*; \w then pour out|strong="H8210"\w* \w the rest|strong="H3605"\w* \w of the blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the base|strong="H3247"\w* \w of the altar|strong="H4196"\w*. \v 13 \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the fat|strong="H2459"\w* \w that covers|strong="H3680"\w* \w the entrails|strong="H7130"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w the lobe|strong="H3508"\w* \w of|strong="H5921"\w* \w the liver|strong="H3516"\w*, \w and both|strong="H8147"\w* \w kidneys|strong="H3629"\w* \w with the fat|strong="H2459"\w* \w on them|strong="H5921"\w*, \w and burn them|strong="H6999"\w* \w on the altar|strong="H4196"\w*. \v 14 \w But|strong="H853"\w* \w burn|strong="H8313"\w* \w the flesh|strong="H1320"\w* \w of the bull|strong="H6499"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w its hide|strong="H5785"\w* \w and dung|strong="H6569"\w* \w outside|strong="H2351"\w* \w the camp|strong="H4264"\w*; \w it is|strong="H1931"\w* \w a sin offering|strong="H2403"\w*.\f + \fr 29:14 \ft Or \fqa purification offering\ft ; also in verse 36\f*
\p \v 15 \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w of the rams|strong="H352"\w*, \w and Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w shall lay|strong="H5564"\w* \w their hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w its|strong="H352"\w* \w head|strong="H7218"\w*. \v 16 \w You are to slaughter|strong="H7819"\w* \w the ram|strong="H352"\w*, \w take|strong="H3947"\w* \w its blood|strong="H1818"\w*, \w and splatter|strong="H2236"\w* \w it on|strong="H5921"\w* \w all sides|strong="H5439"\w* \w of the altar|strong="H4196"\w*. \v 17 \w Cut|strong="H5408"\w* \w the ram|strong="H352"\w* \w into pieces|strong="H5409"\w*, \w wash|strong="H7364"\w* \w the entrails|strong="H7130"\w* \w and legs|strong="H3767"\w*, \w and place them|strong="H5414"\w* \w with|strong="H5921"\w* \w its head|strong="H7218"\w* \w and other pieces|strong="H5409"\w*. \v 18 \w Then burn|strong="H6999"\w* \w the entire|strong="H3605"\w* \w ram|strong="H352"\w* \w on the altar|strong="H4196"\w*; \w it|strong="H1931"\w* \w is a burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w a pleasing|strong="H5207"\w* \w aroma|strong="H7381"\w*, \w a food offering|strong="H801"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 19 \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w the second|strong="H8145"\w* \w ram|strong="H352"\w*, \w and Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w are to lay|strong="H5564"\w* \w their hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w its|strong="H352"\w* \w head|strong="H7218"\w*. \v 20 \w Slaughter|strong="H7819"\w* \w the ram|strong="H352"\w*, \w take|strong="H3947"\w* \w some of its blood|strong="H1818"\w*, \w and put|strong="H5414"\w* \w it on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the right earlobes|strong="H8571"\w* \w of Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and|strong="H5921"\w* \w his sons|strong="H1121"\w*, \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the thumbs|strong="H931"\w* \w of their right|strong="H3233"\w* \w hands|strong="H3027"\w*, \w and on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the big toes|strong="H931"\w* \w of their right|strong="H3233"\w* \w feet|strong="H7272"\w*. \w Splatter|strong="H2236"\w* \w the remaining blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w all sides|strong="H5439"\w* \w of the altar|strong="H4196"\w*. \v 21 \w And take|strong="H3947"\w* \w some of|strong="H4480"\w* \w the blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w and some of the anointing|strong="H4888"\w* \w oil|strong="H8081"\w* \w and sprinkle|strong="H5137"\w* \w it on|strong="H5921"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his garments|strong="H899"\w*, \w as well as on|strong="H5921"\w* \w his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w and their garments|strong="H899"\w*. \w Then he|strong="H1931"\w* \w and his garments|strong="H899"\w* \w will be consecrated|strong="H6942"\w*, \w as well as his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w and their|strong="H1121"\w* \w garments|strong="H899"\w*.
\p \v 22 \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w the fat|strong="H2459"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the ram|strong="H352"\w*, \w the fat tail|strong="H451"\w*, \w the fat|strong="H2459"\w* \w covering|strong="H3680"\w* \w the entrails|strong="H7130"\w*, \w the lobe|strong="H3508"\w* \w of the liver|strong="H3516"\w*, \w both|strong="H8147"\w* \w kidneys|strong="H3629"\w* \w with the fat|strong="H2459"\w* \w on them|strong="H5921"\w*, \w and the right|strong="H3225"\w* \w thigh|strong="H7785"\w* \w (since|strong="H3588"\w* \w this|strong="H1931"\w* \w is a ram|strong="H352"\w* \w for ordination)|strong="H4394"\w*, \v 23 \w along with one|strong="H259"\w* \w loaf|strong="H3603"\w* \w of bread|strong="H3899"\w*, \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w cake|strong="H2471"\w* \w of bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w made with oil|strong="H8081"\w*, \w and one|strong="H259"\w* \w wafer|strong="H7550"\w* \w from the basket|strong="H5536"\w* \w of unleavened bread|strong="H4682"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w is before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \v 24 \w Put|strong="H7760"\w* \w all these|strong="H3605"\w* \w in|strong="H5921"\w* \w the hands|strong="H3709"\w* \w of Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w and wave|strong="H5130"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w as a wave offering|strong="H8573"\w*. \v 25 \w Then take|strong="H3947"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w from their hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w and burn them|strong="H6999"\w* \w on the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w atop|strong="H5921"\w* \w the burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w as a pleasing|strong="H5207"\w* \w aroma|strong="H7381"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*; \w it|strong="H1931"\w* \w is a food offering|strong="H801"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 26 \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w the breast|strong="H2373"\w* \w of the ram|strong="H352"\w* \w of Aaron’s|strong="H175"\w* \w ordination|strong="H4394"\w* \w and wave|strong="H5130"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w as a wave offering|strong="H8573"\w*, \w and it will be|strong="H1961"\w* your \w portion|strong="H4490"\w*. \v 27 \w Consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w for Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w the breast|strong="H2373"\w* \w of the wave offering|strong="H8573"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w is waved|strong="H5130"\w* \w and the thigh|strong="H7785"\w* \w of the heave offering|strong="H8641"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w is lifted up|strong="H7311"\w* \w from the ram|strong="H352"\w* \w of ordination|strong="H4394"\w*. \v 28 \w This will belong to|strong="H1961"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w as a regular|strong="H5769"\w* \w portion|strong="H2706"\w* \w from the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w it|strong="H1931"\w* \w is the heave offering|strong="H8641"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w will make|strong="H8641"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w from their peace offerings|strong="H8002"\w*.
\p \v 29 \w The holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w garments|strong="H899"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w belong to Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w will belong|strong="H1961"\w* \w to his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w after him|strong="H310"\w*, \w so they can be anointed|strong="H4888"\w* \w and ordained|strong="H4390"\w* \w in them|strong="H3027"\w*. \v 30 \w The son|strong="H1121"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w succeeds him|strong="H8478"\w* \w as priest|strong="H3548"\w* \w and enters|strong="H935"\w* \w the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w* \w to minister|strong="H8334"\w* \w in the Holy Place|strong="H6944"\w* \w must wear them|strong="H3847"\w* \w for seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w*.
\s1 Food for the Priests
\p \v 31 \w You are to take|strong="H3947"\w* \w the ram|strong="H352"\w* \w of ordination|strong="H4394"\w* \w and boil|strong="H1310"\w* \w its flesh|strong="H1320"\w* \w in a holy|strong="H6918"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w*. \v 32 \w At the entrance|strong="H6607"\w* \w to the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w*, \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w are to eat|strong="H398"\w* \w the meat|strong="H1320"\w* \w of the ram|strong="H352"\w* \w and the bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w that is|strong="H834"\w* \w in the basket|strong="H5536"\w*. \v 33 \w They must eat|strong="H398"\w* \w those things by which|strong="H834"\w* \w atonement was made|strong="H3722"\w* \w for their ordination|strong="H4390"\w* \w and consecration|strong="H6942"\w*. \w But no|strong="H3808"\w* \w outsider|strong="H2114"\w* \w may eat them|strong="H398"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w these|strong="H1992"\w* \w things are sacred|strong="H6944"\w*. \v 34 \w And if|strong="H518"\w* \w any of|strong="H4480"\w* \w the meat|strong="H1320"\w* \w of ordination|strong="H4394"\w* \w or any bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w is left|strong="H3498"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w the morning|strong="H1242"\w*, \w you are to burn up|strong="H8313"\w* \w the remainder|strong="H3498"\w*. \w It must not|strong="H3808"\w* \w be eaten|strong="H398"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w it|strong="H1931"\w* \w is sacred|strong="H6944"\w*.
\p \v 35 \w This is what|strong="H3602"\w* \w you are to do|strong="H6213"\w* \w for Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w based on all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w I have commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w you|strong="H853"\w*, \w taking seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w to ordain|strong="H4390"\w* \w them|strong="H3027"\w*. \v 36 \w Sacrifice|strong="H6213"\w* \w a bull|strong="H6499"\w* \w as a sin offering|strong="H2403"\w* \w each day|strong="H3117"\w* \w for|strong="H5921"\w* \w atonement|strong="H3725"\w*. \w Purify|strong="H2398"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w by making atonement|strong="H3722"\w* \w for it|strong="H5921"\w*, \w and anoint|strong="H4886"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w* \w to consecrate it|strong="H6942"\w*. \v 37 \w For seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w you shall make atonement|strong="H3722"\w* \w for|strong="H5921"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w and consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w*. \w Then the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w will become|strong="H1961"\w* \w most holy|strong="H6944"\w*; \w whatever|strong="H3605"\w* \w touches|strong="H5060"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w will be holy|strong="H6942"\w*.
\s1 The Daily Offerings
\r (\ref Numbers 28:1–8|NUM 28:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 38 \w This|strong="H2088"\w* \w is what|strong="H834"\w* \w you are to offer|strong="H6213"\w* \w regularly|strong="H8548"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w*, \w each day|strong="H3117"\w*: \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w lambs|strong="H3532"\w* \w that are a year old|strong="H1121"\w*. \v 39 \w Offer|strong="H6213"\w* \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w lamb|strong="H3532"\w* \w in the morning|strong="H1242"\w* \w and the other|strong="H8145"\w* \w at|strong="H996"\w* \w twilight|strong="H6153"\w*.\f + \fr 29:39 \ft Hebrew \fqa between the two evenings\ft ; also in verse 41\f* \v 40 \w With the first|strong="H259"\w* \w lamb|strong="H3532"\w* \w offer a tenth of an ephah|strong="H6241"\w* \w of fine flour|strong="H5560"\w*,\f + \fr 29:40 \fqa A tenth of an ephah\ft is \ref approximately 2|2\ref* dry quarts or 2.2 liters (probably about 2.6 pounds or 1.2 kilograms of flour).\f* \w mixed|strong="H1101"\w* \w with a quarter|strong="H7253"\w* \w hin|strong="H1969"\w* \w of oil|strong="H8081"\w* \w from pressed olives|strong="H3795"\w*,\f + \fr 29:40 \ft Hebrew \fqa a quarter hin of pressed oil\ft ; that is, \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.97 quarts or 0.92 liters\f* \w and a drink offering|strong="H5262"\w* \w of a quarter|strong="H7243"\w* \w hin|strong="H1969"\w* \w of wine|strong="H3196"\w*. \v 41 \w And|strong="H853"\w* \w offer|strong="H6213"\w* \w the second|strong="H8145"\w* \w lamb|strong="H3532"\w* \w at|strong="H996"\w* \w twilight|strong="H6153"\w* \w with|strong="H6213"\w* the same \w grain offering|strong="H4503"\w* \w and drink offering|strong="H5262"\w* \w as in the morning|strong="H1242"\w*, \w as a pleasing|strong="H5207"\w* \w aroma|strong="H7381"\w*, \w a food offering|strong="H801"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 42 \w For the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*, \w this burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w shall be made regularly|strong="H8548"\w* \w at the entrance|strong="H6607"\w* \w to the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w where|strong="H834"\w* \w I will meet|strong="H3259"\w* you \w to speak|strong="H1696"\w* \w with you|strong="H413"\w*. \v 43 \w I will also meet|strong="H3259"\w* \w with the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*, \w and that place will be consecrated|strong="H6942"\w* \w by My glory|strong="H3519"\w*. \v 44 \w So I will consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w* \w and the altar|strong="H4196"\w*, \w and I will consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w to serve Me as priests|strong="H3547"\w*.
\s1 God Will Dwell among the People
\p \v 45 \w Then I will dwell|strong="H7931"\w* \w among|strong="H8432"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and be|strong="H1961"\w* their \w God|strong="H430"\w*. \v 46 \w And they will know|strong="H3045"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w their God|strong="H430"\w*, \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w brought them out|strong="H3318"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w* \w so that I might dwell|strong="H7931"\w* \w among them|strong="H8432"\w*.
\p \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w their God|strong="H430"\w*.[’’]
\c 30
\s1 The Altar of Incense
\r (\ref Exodus 37:25–29|EXO 37:25-29\ref*)
\p \v 1 “\w You are also to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w an altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w* \w for the burning|strong="H4729"\w* \w of incense|strong="H7004"\w*. \v 2 \w It is to be|strong="H1961"\w* \w square|strong="H7251"\w*, \w a cubit|strong="H520"\w* \w long|strong="H753"\w*, \w a cubit|strong="H520"\w* \w wide|strong="H7341"\w*, \w and two cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w high|strong="H6967"\w*.\f + \fr 30:2 \ft The altar was \ref approximately 1|1\ref*.5 feet in length and width, and 3 feet high (45.7 centimeters in length and width, and 91.4 centimeters high).\f* \w Its horns|strong="H7161"\w* \w must be of one piece|strong="H4480"\w*. \v 3 \w Overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w with pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w the top|strong="H1406"\w* \w and all|strong="H5439"\w* \w the sides|strong="H7023"\w* \w and horns|strong="H7161"\w*, \w and make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a molding|strong="H2213"\w* \w of gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w around it|strong="H5439"\w*. \v 4 \w And make|strong="H6213"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w rings|strong="H2885"\w* \w below|strong="H8478"\w* \w the molding|strong="H2213"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w opposite sides|strong="H6654"\w* \w to|strong="H1961"\w* \w hold|strong="H1004"\w* \w the poles|strong="H905"\w* \w used to carry it|strong="H5375"\w*. \v 5 \w Make|strong="H6213"\w* \w the poles|strong="H905"\w* \w of acacia|strong="H7848"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w* \w and overlay|strong="H6823"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w with gold|strong="H2091"\w*.
\p \v 6 \w Place|strong="H5414"\w* \w the altar|strong="H853"\w* \w in front|strong="H6440"\w* \w of the veil|strong="H6532"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w is before|strong="H5921"\w* \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*\f + \fr 30:6 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\ft ; also in verse 26\f*— \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the mercy seat|strong="H3727"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w is over|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*— \w where|strong="H834"\w* \w I will meet|strong="H3259"\w* with you. \v 7 \w And Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w is to burn|strong="H6999"\w* \w fragrant|strong="H5561"\w* \w incense|strong="H7004"\w* \w on it|strong="H5921"\w* \w every morning|strong="H1242"\w* \w when he tends|strong="H3190"\w* \w the lamps|strong="H5216"\w*. \v 8 \w When Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w sets up|strong="H5927"\w* \w the lamps|strong="H5216"\w* \w at|strong="H996"\w* \w twilight|strong="H6153"\w*,\f + \fr 30:8 \ft Hebrew \fqa between the two evenings\f* \w he must burn|strong="H6999"\w* \w the incense|strong="H7004"\w* \w perpetually|strong="H8548"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*. \v 9 \w On this altar|strong="H5921"\w* \w you must not|strong="H3808"\w* \w offer|strong="H5927"\w* \w unauthorized|strong="H2114"\w*\f + \fr 30:9 \ft Or \fqa strange\f* \w incense|strong="H7004"\w* \w or a burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w or grain offering|strong="H4503"\w*; \w nor are you|strong="H3808"\w* \w to pour|strong="H5258"\w* \w a drink offering|strong="H5262"\w* \w on it|strong="H5921"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w Once|strong="H259"\w* \w a year|strong="H8141"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w shall make atonement|strong="H3722"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the horns of the altar|strong="H7161"\w*. \w Throughout your generations|strong="H1755"\w* \w he shall make atonement|strong="H3722"\w* \w on it|strong="H5921"\w* \w annually|strong="H259"\w* \w with the blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w of the sin offering|strong="H2403"\w*\f + \fr 30:10 \ft Or \fqa purification offering\f* \w of atonement|strong="H3725"\w*. \w The altar is|strong="H1931"\w* \w most|strong="H6944"\w* \w holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.”
\s1 The Census Offering
\r (\ref 2 Samuel 24:1–9|2SA 24:1-9\ref*; \ref 1 Chronicles 21:1–6|1CH 21:1-6\ref*)
\p \v 11 \w Then the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \v 12 “\w When|strong="H3588"\w* \w you take a census|strong="H5375"\w* \w of the Israelites|strong="H3478"\w* \w to number them|strong="H6485"\w*, \w each man|strong="H376"\w* \w must pay|strong="H5414"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w a ransom|strong="H3724"\w* \w for his life|strong="H5315"\w* \w when he is counted|strong="H6485"\w*. \w Then no|strong="H3808"\w* \w plague|strong="H5063"\w* \w will come|strong="H1961"\w* upon them \w when they are numbered|strong="H6485"\w*. \v 13 \w Everyone|strong="H3605"\w* \w who crosses|strong="H5674"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w to those counted|strong="H6485"\w* \w must pay|strong="H5414"\w* \w a half|strong="H4276"\w* \w shekel|strong="H8255"\w*,\f + \fr 30:13 \fqa A half shekel\ft is \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.2 ounces or 5.7 grams; also in verse 15.\f* \w according to the sanctuary|strong="H6944"\w* \w shekel|strong="H8255"\w*, \w which weighs|strong="H8255"\w* \w twenty|strong="H6242"\w* \w gerahs|strong="H1626"\w*.\f + \fr 30:13 \fqa \ref 20|0\ref* gerahs\ft is equivalent to one shekel \ref (approximately 0|0\ref*.4 ounces or 11.4 grams).\f* \w This half|strong="H4276"\w* \w shekel|strong="H8255"\w* \w is an offering|strong="H8641"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \v 14 \w Everyone|strong="H3605"\w* \w twenty years|strong="H6242"\w* \w of age|strong="H1121"\w* \w or older|strong="H4605"\w* \w who crosses|strong="H5674"\w* \w over|strong="H5921"\w* \w must give|strong="H5414"\w* \w this offering|strong="H8641"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \v 15 \w In making|strong="H5414"\w* \w the offering|strong="H8641"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w to atone|strong="H3722"\w* \w for|strong="H5921"\w* \w your lives|strong="H5315"\w*, \w the rich|strong="H6223"\w* \w shall not|strong="H3808"\w* \w give more|strong="H7235"\w* \w than a half|strong="H4276"\w* \w shekel|strong="H8255"\w*, \w nor shall|strong="H3808"\w* \w the poor|strong="H1800"\w* \w give less|strong="H4591"\w*. \v 16 \w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w the atonement|strong="H3725"\w* \w money|strong="H3701"\w* \w from the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and use|strong="H5414"\w* \w it for|strong="H5921"\w* \w the service|strong="H5656"\w* \w of the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w*. \w It will serve as|strong="H1961"\w* \w a memorial|strong="H2146"\w* \w for the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w to make atonement|strong="H3722"\w* \w for|strong="H5921"\w* \w your lives|strong="H5315"\w*.”
\s1 The Bronze Basin
\r (\ref Exodus 38:8|EXO 38:8\ref*)
\p \v 17 \w And the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \v 18 “\w You are to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w basin|strong="H3595"\w* \w with a bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w stand|strong="H3653"\w* \w for washing|strong="H7364"\w*. \w Set|strong="H5414"\w* \w it between|strong="H996"\w* \w the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w* \w and the altar|strong="H4196"\w*, \w and put|strong="H5414"\w* \w water|strong="H4325"\w* \w in it|strong="H8033"\w*, \v 19 \w with which|strong="H4480"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w are to wash|strong="H7364"\w* \w their hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w and feet|strong="H7272"\w*. \v 20 \w Whenever they enter|strong="H935"\w* \w the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w approach|strong="H5066"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w to minister|strong="H8334"\w* \w by presenting|strong="H6999"\w* \w a food offering|strong="H801"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w they must wash|strong="H7364"\w* \w with water|strong="H4325"\w* \w so that they will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w die|strong="H4191"\w*. \v 21 \w Thus they are to wash|strong="H7364"\w* \w their hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w and feet|strong="H7272"\w* \w so that they will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w die|strong="H4191"\w*; \w this shall be|strong="H1961"\w* \w a permanent|strong="H5769"\w* \w statute|strong="H2706"\w* \w for Aaron and his descendants|strong="H2233"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*.”
\s1 The Anointing Oil
\p \v 22 \w Then the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \v 23 “\w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w the finest|strong="H7218"\w* \w spices|strong="H1314"\w*: \w 500 shekels|strong="H2568"\w* \w of liquid|strong="H1865"\w* \w myrrh|strong="H4753"\w*,\f + \fr 30:23 \fqa \ref 500|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 12|12\ref*.6 pounds or 5.7 kilograms of myrrh.\f* \w half that amount|strong="H4276"\w* \w (250 shekels)|strong="H2572"\w* \w of fragrant|strong="H1314"\w* \w cinnamon|strong="H7076"\w*,\f + \fr 30:23 \fqa \ref 250|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 6|6\ref*.3 pounds or 2.9 kilograms of cinnamon.\f* \w 250 shekels|strong="H2572"\w* \w of fragrant|strong="H1314"\w* \w cane|strong="H7070"\w*,\f + \fr 30:23 \fqa \ref 250|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 6|6\ref*.3 pounds or 2.9 kilograms of cane.\f* \v 24 \w 500 shekels|strong="H2568"\w* \w of cassia|strong="H6916"\w*\f + \fr 30:24 \fqa \ref 500|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 12|12\ref*.6 pounds or 5.7 kilograms of cassia.\f* — \w all according to the sanctuary|strong="H6944"\w* \w shekel|strong="H8255"\w* — \w and a hin|strong="H1969"\w* \w of olive|strong="H2132"\w* \w oil|strong="H8081"\w*.\f + \fr 30:24 \fqa A hin\ft is \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.97 gallons or 3.67 liters of olive oil.\f* \v 25 \w Prepare|strong="H6213"\w* \w from these a sacred|strong="H6944"\w* \w anointing|strong="H4888"\w* \w oil|strong="H8081"\w*, \w a fragrant blend|strong="H7545"\w*, \w the work|strong="H4639"\w* \w of a perfumer|strong="H7543"\w*; \w it will be|strong="H1961"\w* \w a sacred|strong="H6944"\w* \w anointing|strong="H4888"\w* \w oil|strong="H8081"\w*.
\p \v 26 \w Use this oil to anoint|strong="H4886"\w* \w the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w*, \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*, \v 27 \w the table|strong="H7979"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w its utensils|strong="H3627"\w*, \w the lampstand|strong="H4501"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w its utensils|strong="H3627"\w*, \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w of incense|strong="H7004"\w*, \v 28 \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w of burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w its utensils|strong="H3627"\w*, \w and the basin|strong="H3595"\w* \w with its stand|strong="H3653"\w*. \v 29 \w You are to consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w so that they will be|strong="H1961"\w* \w most|strong="H6944"\w* \w holy|strong="H6944"\w*. \w Whatever|strong="H3605"\w* \w touches|strong="H5060"\w* them \w shall be holy|strong="H6942"\w*. \v 30 \w Anoint|strong="H4886"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w and consecrate|strong="H6942"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w to serve Me as priests|strong="H3547"\w*.
\p \v 31 \w And you are to tell|strong="H1696"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*, ‘\w This|strong="H2088"\w* \w will be|strong="H1961"\w* My \w sacred|strong="H6944"\w* \w anointing|strong="H4888"\w* \w oil|strong="H8081"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*. \v 32 \w It must not|strong="H3808"\w* \w be used to anoint|strong="H5480"\w* \w an ordinary man|strong="H120"\w*, \w and you must not|strong="H3808"\w* \w make|strong="H6213"\w* \w anything like it|strong="H3644"\w* \w with the same formula|strong="H4971"\w*. \w It|strong="H1931"\w* \w is holy|strong="H6944"\w*, \w and it must be|strong="H1961"\w* \w holy|strong="H6944"\w* to you. \v 33 \w Anyone|strong="H376"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w mixes perfume|strong="H7543"\w* \w like it|strong="H3644"\w* \w or puts|strong="H5414"\w* \w it on|strong="H5921"\w* \w an outsider|strong="H2114"\w* \w shall be cut off|strong="H3772"\w* \w from his people|strong="H5971"\w*.’”
\s1 The Incense
\p \v 34 \w The LORD also|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, “\w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w fragrant spices|strong="H5561"\w* — \w gum resin|strong="H5198"\w*, \w onycha|strong="H7827"\w*, \w galbanum|strong="H2464"\w*, \w and pure|strong="H2134"\w* \w frankincense|strong="H3828"\w* — \w in equal measures|strong="H905"\w*, \v 35 \w and make|strong="H6213"\w* \w a fragrant blend of incense|strong="H7004"\w*, \w the work of a perfumer|strong="H7543"\w*, \w seasoned with salt|strong="H4414"\w*, \w pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w and holy|strong="H6944"\w*. \v 36 \w Grind|strong="H7833"\w* \w some of it|strong="H4480"\w* \w into fine powder|strong="H1854"\w* \w and place|strong="H5414"\w* \w it|strong="H4480"\w* \w in front of|strong="H6440"\w* \w the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*\f + \fr 30:36 \fqa The Testimony \ft refers to the stone tablets in the ark of the covenant inscribed with the Ten Commandments.\f* \w in the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w*, \w where|strong="H834"\w* \w I will meet|strong="H3259"\w* with you. \w It shall be|strong="H1961"\w* \w most|strong="H6944"\w* \w holy|strong="H6944"\w* to you. \v 37 \w You are never to use|strong="H6213"\w* \w this formula|strong="H4971"\w* \w to make|strong="H6213"\w* \w incense|strong="H7004"\w* for yourselves; \w you shall regard it as holy|strong="H6944"\w* to \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \v 38 \w Anyone|strong="H376"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w makes|strong="H6213"\w* \w something like|strong="H3644"\w* \w it to enjoy|strong="H7306"\w* its fragrance \w shall be cut off|strong="H3772"\w* \w from his people|strong="H5971"\w*.”
\c 31
\s1 Bezalel and Oholiab
\r (\ref Exodus 35:30–35|EXO 35:30-35\ref*)
\p \v 1 \w Then the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \v 2 “\w See|strong="H7200"\w*, \w I have called|strong="H7121"\w* \w by name|strong="H8034"\w* \w Bezalel|strong="H1212"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Uri|strong="H221"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Hur|strong="H2354"\w*, \w of the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*. \v 3 \w And I have filled|strong="H4390"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w with the Spirit|strong="H7307"\w* \w of God|strong="H430"\w*, \w with skill|strong="H2451"\w*, \w ability|strong="H8394"\w*, \w and knowledge|strong="H1847"\w* \w in all kinds|strong="H3605"\w* \w of craftsmanship|strong="H4399"\w*, \v 4 \w to design|strong="H2803"\w* \w artistic|strong="H4284"\w* \w works|strong="H6213"\w* \w in gold|strong="H2091"\w*, \w silver|strong="H3701"\w*, \w and bronze|strong="H5178"\w*, \v 5 \w to cut|strong="H2799"\w* \w gemstones|strong="H68"\w* \w for settings|strong="H4390"\w*, \w and to carve|strong="H2799"\w* \w wood|strong="H6086"\w*, \w so that he may be a master|strong="H6213"\w* \w of every|strong="H3605"\w* \w craft|strong="H4399"\w*.
\p \v 6 \w Moreover, I|strong="H589"\w* \w have selected|strong="H5414"\w* \w Oholiab|strong="H171"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Ahisamach|strong="H294"\w*, \w of the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Dan|strong="H1835"\w*, \w as his assistant|strong="H854"\w*.
\p \w I have also given|strong="H5414"\w* \w skill|strong="H2451"\w* \w to all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the craftsmen|strong="H2450"\w*, \w that they may fashion|strong="H6213"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w I have commanded you|strong="H6680"\w*: \v 7 \w the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w*, \w the ark|strong="H727"\w* \w of the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*\f + \fr 31:7 \ft That is, \fqa the ark of the covenant\f* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w the mercy seat|strong="H3727"\w* \w upon it|strong="H5921"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the other furnishings|strong="H3627"\w* \w of the tent|strong="H168"\w*— \v 8 \w the table|strong="H7979"\w* \w with its utensils|strong="H3627"\w*, \w the pure|strong="H2889"\w* \w gold lampstand|strong="H4501"\w* \w with all|strong="H3605"\w* \w its utensils|strong="H3627"\w*, \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w of incense|strong="H7004"\w*, \v 9 \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w* \w of burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w with all|strong="H3605"\w* \w its utensils|strong="H3627"\w*, \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w the basin|strong="H3595"\w* \w with its stand|strong="H3653"\w*— \v 10 \w as well as|strong="H853"\w* \w the woven|strong="H8278"\w* \w garments|strong="H899"\w*, \w both the holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w garments|strong="H899"\w* \w for Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w the priest|strong="H3548"\w* \w and the garments|strong="H899"\w* \w for his sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w to serve as priests|strong="H3547"\w*, \v 11 \w in addition to|strong="H853"\w* \w the anointing|strong="H4888"\w* \w oil|strong="H8081"\w* \w and fragrant|strong="H5561"\w* \w incense|strong="H7004"\w* \w for the Holy Place|strong="H6944"\w*. \w They are to make them|strong="H6213"\w* \w according to all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w I have commanded you|strong="H6680"\w*.”
\s1 The Sign of the Sabbath
\r (\ref Numbers 15:32–36|NUM 15:32-36\ref*)
\p \v 12 \w And the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \v 13 “\w Tell|strong="H1696"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*, ‘\w Surely|strong="H389"\w* \w you must keep|strong="H8104"\w* \w My Sabbaths|strong="H7676"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w this|strong="H1931"\w* \w will be a sign|strong="H226"\w* \w between Me|strong="H996"\w* \w and you|strong="H996"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*, \w so that you may know|strong="H3045"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w who sanctifies you|strong="H6942"\w*. \v 14 \w Keep|strong="H8104"\w* \w the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w it|strong="H1931"\w* \w is holy|strong="H6944"\w* to you. \w Anyone who profanes it|strong="H2490"\w* \w must surely be put to death|strong="H4191"\w*. \w Whoever|strong="H3605"\w* \w does|strong="H6213"\w* \w any work|strong="H4399"\w* on that day \w must be cut off|strong="H3772"\w* \w from among|strong="H7130"\w* \w his people|strong="H5971"\w*. \v 15 \w For six|strong="H8337"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w work|strong="H4399"\w* \w may be done|strong="H6213"\w*, \w but the seventh|strong="H7637"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w is a Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w* \w of complete rest|strong="H7677"\w*, \w holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \w Whoever|strong="H3605"\w* \w does|strong="H6213"\w* \w any work|strong="H4399"\w* \w on the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w must surely be put to death|strong="H4191"\w*.
\p \v 16 \w The Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w must keep|strong="H8104"\w* \w the Sabbath|strong="H7676"\w*, \w celebrating|strong="H6213"\w* \w it|strong="H7676"\w* \w as a permanent|strong="H5769"\w* \w covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H1755"\w*. \v 17 \w It|strong="H1931"\w* \w is a sign|strong="H226"\w* \w between Me|strong="H996"\w* \w and the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w forever|strong="H5769"\w*; \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w in six|strong="H8337"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w made|strong="H6213"\w* \w the heavens|strong="H8064"\w* \w and the earth|strong="H776"\w*, \w but on the seventh|strong="H7637"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w He rested|strong="H7673"\w* \w and was refreshed|strong="H5314"\w*.’”
\s1 Moses Receives the Tablets
\p \v 18 \w When the LORD had finished|strong="H3615"\w* \w speaking|strong="H1696"\w* \w with Moses|strong="H854"\w* \w on Mount|strong="H2022"\w* \w Sinai|strong="H5514"\w*, \w He gave|strong="H5414"\w* \w him|strong="H4872"\w* \w the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w tablets|strong="H3871"\w* \w of the Testimony|strong="H5715"\w*, \w tablets|strong="H3871"\w* \w of stone|strong="H68"\w* \w inscribed|strong="H3789"\w* \w by the finger|strong="H676"\w* \w of God|strong="H430"\w*.
\c 32
\s1 The Golden Calf
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 9:7–29|DEU 9:7-29\ref*; \ref Acts 7:39–43|ACT 7:39-43\ref*)
\p \v 1 \w Now when the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w was delayed|strong="H954"\w* \w in coming down|strong="H3381"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the mountain|strong="H2022"\w*, \w they|strong="H5971"\w* \w gathered|strong="H6950"\w* \w around|strong="H5921"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Come|strong="H6965"\w*, \w make|strong="H6213"\w* us \w gods|strong="H430"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w will go|strong="H1980"\w* \w before us|strong="H6440"\w*. \w As for|strong="H3588"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w brought us up|strong="H5927"\w* \w out of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*, \w we do not|strong="H3808"\w* \w know|strong="H3045"\w* \w what|strong="H4100"\w* \w has happened|strong="H1961"\w* to him!”\f + \fr 32:1 \ft Cited in \ref Acts 7:40|ACT 7:40\ref*\f*
\p \v 2 \w So Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w told|strong="H559"\w* \w them|strong="H413"\w*, “\w Take off|strong="H6561"\w* \w the gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w earrings|strong="H5141"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w are on|strong="H241"\w* \w your wives|strong="H802"\w* \w and sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w and daughters|strong="H1323"\w*, \w and bring them|strong="H935"\w* \w to me|strong="H413"\w*.”
\p \v 3 \w Then all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w took off|strong="H6561"\w* \w their gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w earrings|strong="H5141"\w* \w and brought them|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w*. \v 4 \w He took the gold|strong="H3947"\w* \w from their hands|strong="H3027"\w*, \w and|strong="H6696"\w* \w with an engraving tool|strong="H2747"\w* \w he fashioned|strong="H6213"\w* \w it|strong="H853"\w* \w into a molten|strong="H4541"\w* \w calf|strong="H5695"\w*. \w And they said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w These|strong="H428"\w*, \w O Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w are your gods|strong="H430"\w*, \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w brought you up|strong="H5927"\w* \w out of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*!”
