\p \v 22 And you \w are to celebrate|strong="H6213"\w* \w the Feast|strong="H2282"\w* \w of Weeks|strong="H7620"\w*\f + \fr 34:22 \ft That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as \fqa the Feast of Harvest\ft (see \ref Exodus 23:16|EXO 23:16\ref*) or \fqa the Feast of Pentecost\ft (see \ref Acts 2:1|ACT 2:1\ref*).\f* \w with the firstfruits|strong="H1061"\w* \w of the wheat|strong="H2406"\w* \w harvest|strong="H7105"\w*, \w and the Feast|strong="H2282"\w* \w of Ingathering|strong="H614"\w*\f + \fr 34:22 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is later called \fqa the Feast of Tabernacles \ft (or \fqa Booths \ft or \fqa Shelters\ft ).\f* \w at the turn|strong="H8622"\w* \w of the year|strong="H8141"\w*. \v 23 \w Three|strong="H7969"\w* \w times|strong="H6471"\w* \w a year|strong="H8141"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w your males|strong="H2138"\w* \w are to appear|strong="H7200"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the Lord|strong="H113"\w* \w GOD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \v 24 \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w I will drive out|strong="H3423"\w* \w the nations|strong="H1471"\w* \w before you|strong="H6440"\w* \w and enlarge|strong="H7337"\w* \w your borders|strong="H1366"\w*, \w and no|strong="H3808"\w* \w one|strong="H376"\w* \w will covet|strong="H2530"\w* \w your land|strong="H776"\w* \w when you go up|strong="H5927"\w* \w three|strong="H7969"\w* \w times|strong="H6471"\w* \w a year|strong="H8141"\w* \w to appear|strong="H7200"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w your God|strong="H430"\w*.
\p \v 25 \w Do not|strong="H3808"\w* \w offer|strong="H7819"\w* \w the blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w of a sacrifice to Me|strong="H2077"\w* \w along with|strong="H5921"\w* \w anything leavened|strong="H2557"\w*, \w and do not let|strong="H3808"\w* \w any of the sacrifice|strong="H2077"\w* \w from the Passover|strong="H6453"\w* \w Feast|strong="H2282"\w* \w remain|strong="H3885"\w* \w until morning|strong="H1242"\w*.
